# Feature Folder Structure

Every feature lives under `src/features/<feature-name>/`. No exceptions.

## Required structure

```
src/features/<feature>/
├── index.ts              ← barrel: only public exports consumed outside this feature
├── types.ts              ← plain TypeScript types (no runtime code, no imports from zod)
├── schema.ts             ← Zod schemas + inferred types (only used inside the feature)
├── service.ts            ← all API calls (apiClient.*). No UI, no hooks.
├── hooks/
│   └── use<Feature>.ts   ← state orchestration (useQuery, useMutation, useState, useForm)
└── components/
    ├── <Feature>Page.tsx     ← composition only: wires hook → components. No logic.
    ├── <Feature>Card.tsx
    └── <Noun>Dialog.tsx
```

## Enforcement

These rules are enforced by ESLint (`eslint.config.js`) — they will fail `npm run lint` and CI for **any IDE, any AI, any developer**:
- `no-restricted-imports` → blocks deep imports from `src/pages/` into feature internals
- `no-restricted-syntax` → blocks `useQuery`, `useMutation`, `useForm`, `useQueryClient` inside `src/pages/`

Run `npm run lint` before every commit.

## Rules

### ✅ DO
- Import between files inside the same feature using relative paths (`./schema`, `../types`)
- Import a feature from outside using only its barrel: `@/features/addresses`
- Keep `types.ts` zero-runtime (only `type` / `interface`, never `z.object`)
- Keep `service.ts` free of React (no hooks, no state)
- Keep page components free of `apiClient`, `useQuery`, `useMutation`
- Export hook intent-named actions (`startCreate`, `closeForm`, `cancelDelete`) — never raw state setters (`setOpen`, `setDeletingId`)

### ❌ NEVER
- Put a feature's schema in `src/lib/validation/` — `lib/validation/` is for **shared cross-feature** schemas only (e.g. auth)
- Put types, service, or hooks directly inside `src/pages/`
- Import from deep inside another feature: `@/features/cart/store/cartSlice` ← use the barrel instead
- Use `any` — always type Axios errors as `AxiosError<unknown>` and cast `response.data` explicitly

## Example: adding a new "reviews" feature

```
src/features/reviews/
├── index.ts
├── types.ts          ← type Review = { id: string; rating: number; ... }
├── schema.ts         ← export const createReviewSchema = z.object({ ... })
├── service.ts        ← export const reviewService = { getAll, create, delete }
├── hooks/
│   └── useManageReviews.ts
└── components/
    ├── ReviewsPage.tsx
    ├── ReviewCard.tsx
    └── ReviewFormDialog.tsx
```

The page entry point stays in `src/pages/reviews/ReviewsPage.tsx` and imports **only** from the barrel:
```ts
import { ReviewsPage } from '@/features/reviews'
```
